	Yes, I realize everyone and their mother has an idea that they'd like
to see thrown into the game.  Here's mine: ;)

	We frequently encounter throne rooms, zoos, etc.  And we all know that
one sure way for less-experienced characters to survive these rooms is a handy-
dandy ring of conflict.  But I'd like to see something nastier...

	One interesting thing from Donaldson's Unbeliever series(es) (serieii?)
is the fighting formation of the ur-viles.  This should be a large group of 
critters (minimum 15), impervious to rings of conflict, that would orient them-
selves such that the apex of the wedge was the only one to be in a fighting
position wrt the player-character.  If the apex guy gets offed, the wedge 
reforms to present a new head nasty.  The level of the apex should decrease
as the wedge is whittled.  Abilities?  How about a sword of disintegration?
This could be picked up by the player (only one, let's have each death cause
some self-disintegration).  Of course, there'd be a fair chance that wielding
it could cause some armor to melt, and stowing it in the pack could trash some
other item(s).  They'd also be able to cast some spells, I'd think.

	Now, obviously, these critters would require a big arena to work in,
which I haven't made an attempt to work out.  That's what we have a DevTeam
for, isn't it??  ;)

